{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T13:57:53.903Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_yStaQX5OS4N5T4hKbAYPWRer","output":"Chunk ID: 95c990\nWall time: 0.4141 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 6488\nOutput:\n{\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire.io/trails/6038b77becfc\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- New `GET /api/v1/me/recap` endpoint returning per-agent rollups (checkpoints, tokens, transcript tokens, files changed, labels, skills, MCP servers, tool mix) for the authenticated user, plus an optional `contributors` counterpart aggregated across every contributor on a scoped repo.\\n- Replaces three separate CLI calls (`GET /me/checkpoints` + `POST /checkpoints/analyses/batch` + `GET /:org/:repo/overview/*`) with one aggregate.\\n- Powers the \\\"you vs. team\\\" columns in `entire recap` (CLI side: entireio/cli#1015).\\n\\n## Behavior\\n\\n- **`?repo=org/name`** — when supplied, both me-side and team-side queries scope to that repo at the SQL level. The response's `contributors` field (top-level + per-agent) carries the team aggregate.\\n- **No `?repo=`** — me-side aggregates span every repo the user has checkpoints on; team-side is **skipped** entirely (no coherent \\\"everyone else\\\" reference frame across repos), and `contributors` is `null`.\\n- **`?since=…&until=…`** — ISO-8601 explicit window, takes precedence over `timeframe`. The CLI uses this so `--day`/`--week`/`--month` line up exactly with the server aggregation window.\\n- **`?timeframe=last-month|last-3-months|last-6-months`** — fallback when explicit dates are absent.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\nThis PR matches the pattern established by /me/activity (#1590): route handler in `api/src/routes/recap.ts` fetches checkpoints + analyses and aggregates qualitative fields (labels/skills/MCP/tool-mix) in JS via `mergeAnalysesInto`. ~1,500 lines, including tests + codegen output.\\n\\n**The perf refactor — denormalizing those qualitative fields into SQL-aggregatable tables — lives in #1737, stacked on this PR.** Splitting keeps each review focused: this one is \\\"add the endpoint,\\\" #1737 is \\\"make it fast.\\\" Both should land before the rollout completes.\\n\\n## Pairs with\\n\\n- CLI side: entireio/cli#1015\\n- Perf follow-up: #1737\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Live smoke vs. local wrangler dev (pointed at staging PlanetScale): `GET /api/v1/me/recap?repo=entireio/cli&since=…&until=…` returns populated agents with labels / skills / toolMix.\\n- [x] `entire recap --view both --insecure-http-auth` (CLI #1015) renders against this endpoint end-to-end.\\n- [x] `pnpm --filter entire-api run typecheck` — clean.\\n- [x] `pnpm --filter entire-api run test:run` — all tests passing.\\n- [x] `pnpm format:check` + `pnpm -r run lint` — clean.\\n\\n## Out of scope (handled in #1737)\\n\\n- Denormalized `repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels` / `_skills` / `_tool_mix` / `_mcp` tables\\n- Worker write path that populates them\\n- Backfill script for existing analyses\\n- SQL `GROUP BY` aggregator replacing `mergeAnalysesInto`\\n- `transcript_tokens` and `files_changed` scalar columns on `repo_checkpoint_analyses`\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-23T03:18:43Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-23T03:18:43Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Consolidates three CLI fetches (me/checkpoints, batch analyses, repo\\noverview) into a single endpoint returning per-agent rollups for both\\nme and contributors sides. Powers the you-vs-team columns in\\n`entire recap`.\\n\\nReturns for every agent the authenticated user has used:\\n- me: checkpoints / labels / skills / mcpServers / toolMix\\n- contributors: same shape aggregated across all contributors to a\\n  ?repo= scoped repo (null otherwise)\\n\\nAlso adds repo_id to the UserCheckpoint shape. getCheckpointsByUser\\nselected it but dropped it in the map; the recap aggregator needs\\nit to pull analyses per-checkpoint on the me side.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): add /api/v1/me/recap for per-agent CLI aggregates\",\"oid\":\"73cee5ada1f97da5ede5a02978b30ceb9a7a714e\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-23T17:50:00Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-23T17:50:00Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Fixes CI format check that was blocking both API and Frontend test jobs.\\nNo behavior change — whitespace-only.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"style(recap): apply oxfmt to api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"oid\":\"b28cb804f2698cb0cc2639705153f83f8a4ab748\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-23T17:53:22Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-23T17:53:22Z\",\"messageBody\":\"CI drift check caught that describeRoute() metadata wasn't reflected\\nin docs/openapi.json. Regenerated via pnpm openapi:generate.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): regenerate OpenAPI spec for /me/recap route\",\"oid\":\"bd670bf294a467d6fde32dcc78e928bcaff97a0b\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-23T17:55:31Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-23T17:55:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Adds the typed client helpers (GetApiV1MeRecapData, GetApiV1MeRecap,\\ngetApiV1MeRecapOptions, etc.) so FE tests' drift check passes.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): regenerate frontend SDK for /me/recap route\",\"oid\":\"b4d4f09587dc41a3e81094910195cbabf7b15b57\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-23T19:36:40Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-23T19:36:40Z\",\"messageBody\":\"# Conflicts:\\n#\\tfrontend/src/gen/api-sdk/index.ts\\n#\\tfrontend/src/gen/api-sdk/react-query.gen.ts\\n#\\tfrontend/src/gen/api-sdk/sdk.gen.ts\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/me-recap-endpoint\",\"oid\":\"4a49e7dfc51d5b467f9c275b7059f42183c77069\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-23T19:43:03Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-23T19:43:03Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/me-recap-endpoint\",\"oid\":\"6fb6eadeb32228d2548d42bcdf27711145d3a084\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-24T01:26:53Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-24T01:26:53Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Before: /me/recap built a parallel aggregation layer (recap-aggregator.ts)\\nover a mix of user-overview and repo-overview queries. Result:\\n- me.tokens always 0 (analyses don't carry tokens)\\n- contributors double-counted the user (no exclusion filter)\\n- response scope asymmetric (me cross-repo, team single-repo)\\n- numbers drifted from entire.io dashboard (separate aggregator)\\n- no per-day activity data (no source)\\n\\nAfter: /me/recap slices the same source (repo_checkpoints joined with\\nrepo_commits) twice with disjoint author filters:\\n- me  = commit_author_github_id == user.github_id (across all repos)\\n- team = commit_author_github_id != user.github_id, scoped to repos\\n        the user is active in (via new getTeamCheckpointsOnUserRepos)\\n\\nPer-agent aggregates come from iterating the checkpoint rows directly\\n(counts, tokens from input_tokens + output_tokens). Analyses merge in\\nlabels/skills/mcpServers/toolMix/transcriptTokens/filesChanged. Daily\\nactivity counts come from the me-side checkpoints bucketed by day.\\n\\nAlso:\\n- Accepts explicit ?since= and ?until= ISO params so the CLI can pass\\n  its exact range bounds (no more 'ask for today, get 30 days').\\n- Returns 'daily' array in the response body so the CLI activity strip\\n  uses server-computed counts instead of local-only data.\\n- Deletes recap-aggregator.ts (181 lines) — the parallel aggregation is\\n  replaced by direct row iteration.\\n\\nResult: CLI me-side matches the entire.io /me dashboard. Team column\\nis 'other humans working on your repos' — cross-repo, clean semantics,\\nno double-count. Token numbers real. Activity strip reflects server\\ntruth.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"refactor(recap): rewrite /me/recap on shared source-of-truth queries\",\"oid\":\"c1a51c52011c998de6f345a20c5c60878fcc0197\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-24T01:49:20Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-24T01:49:20Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Declares since/until/daily in recapResponseSchema and regenerates\\napi/docs/openapi.json + frontend SDK so the drift-check CI passes.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): update response schema + regenerate OpenAPI + SDK\",\"oid\":\"b7dd37d2ff5c6bec0ab8987eaa46f078e97f3c4b\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-27T14:06:54Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-27T14:06:54Z\",\"messageBody\":\"mergeAnalysesInto runs once per side; the two sides operate on disjoint\\ncheckpoint sets (different repos × different authors), so the calls can\\nsafely run in parallel via Promise.all instead of awaiting them in\\nsequence. Saves one full round of analysis lookups (~200-300ms in prod,\\nmore under hot-cache misses) per /me/recap request.\\n\\nFollow-up: aggregate team-side counts in SQL instead of fetching up to\\n1000 rows of full checkpoint metadata then aggregating in JS — see\\ninternal perf notes.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"perf(recap): parallelize me/team analysis merges\",\"oid\":\"8f571f53af52170cba8b19473e1fbbcee5d9d788\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-27T14:52:13Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-27T14:52:13Z\",\"messageBody\":\"# Conflicts:\\n#\\tapi/docs/openapi.json\\n#\\tfrontend/src/gen/api-sdk/index.ts\\n#\\tfrontend/src/gen/api-sdk/react-query.gen.ts\\n#\\tfrontend/src/gen/api-sdk/sdk.gen.ts\\n#\\tfrontend/src/gen/api-sdk/types.gen.ts\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/me-recap-endpoint\",\"oid\":\"ab8f91ae62ba8e4fd12af6b82a2cb6ffbf3bf284\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-27T16:00:17Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-27T16:00:17Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Bundles the eight findings from the Copilot review on this PR.\\n\\nCorrectness:\\n- Push the ?repo= filter into both getCheckpointsByUser and\\n  getTeamCheckpointsOnUserRepos at the SQL level. The previous post-\\n  filter in JS could drop relevant checkpoints when cross-repo activity\\n  pushed the requested repo's rows out of LIMIT 500 before the filter\\n  saw them.\\n- Count distinctUsers by commit_author_github_id, not by commit_sha.\\n  The old commit_sha-based count conflated \\\"team has 50 commits this\\n  week\\\" with \\\"50 distinct contributors\\\" — wrong by an order of\\n  magnitude on active repos. UserCheckpoint now carries\\n  commit_author_github_id end-to-end so the route can do an authoritative\\n  Set count.\\n- Key analyses by ${repo_id}:${checkpoint_id} instead of just\\n  checkpoint_id. checkpoint_id is unique per repo, not globally\\n  (uq_repo_checkpoints_repo_checkpoint enforces (repo_id, checkpoint_id)),\\n  so cross-repo recap could overwrite an analysis with one from a\\n  different repo that happened to share the same checkpoint_id.\\n\\nSpec alignment:\\n- Skip getTeamOnUserRepos entirely when ?repo= is absent and return\\n  contributors:null (both top-level and per-agent), matching the\\n  documented contract that team aggregation only makes sense scoped to\\n  a single repo.\\n- Document since/until query params in the route describeRoute /\\n  OpenAPI schema. The CLI relies on these for --day/--week/--month\\n  bounds; the prior implementation honored them but didn't document\\n  them, so the SDK/clients had no way to discover them.\\n\\nDoc rot:\\n- Header comment claimed tokens were \\\"intentionally omitted\\\" but they\\n  were always in the response. Update the comment to match.\\n\\nTests:\\n- New api/src/routes/recap.test.ts pins the five behavioral guarantees:\\n  null contributors when no ?repo=, repoFullName threading into both\\n  underlying queries, distinct-author counting, since/until override,\\n  and per-(repo_id, checkpoint_id) analysis attribution.\\n\\nGenerated artifacts:\\n- api/docs/openapi.json + frontend/src/gen/api-sdk/types.gen.ts\\n  regenerated from the new describeRoute parameters list.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(recap): address Copilot PR review on /me/recap\",\"oid\":\"199878aa07d1b9f3c86aae781a2889e6f2d45598\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T14:53:15Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-29T14:53:15Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/me-recap-endpoint\",\"oid\":\"e3b0025f361235d3cb0aacbb5398500b768edfd1\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T15:03:50Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-29T15:03:50Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/me-recap-endpoint\",\"oid\":\"363d69b265fcab4cf531efdafecf5aa74ed50067\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T15:45:37Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-29T15:45:37Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…f silent fallbacks\\n\\n- parseRecapWindow now returns 400 for partial/invalid since/until and inverted\\n  ranges, replacing a silent fallback to the default 6-month window.\\n- Malformed analysis_json rows now record a span error and log instead of\\n  being dropped without a trace, so we don't ship systematically understated\\n  per-agent labels/skills/toolMix without operator visibility.\\n- buildDailyActivity parses commit_date as UTC instead of slicing the raw\\n  string, fixing mis-bucketing for offset-formatted timestamps.\\n- Adds integration tests for getTeamCheckpointsOnUserRepos covering both\\n  the team/me exclusion and the \\\"scoped to user's active repos\\\" contract,\\n  closing the gap on a previously untested net-new function.\\n- OpenAPI 404 description corrected (only user-not-found is emitted).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(recap): surface validation, parse, and bucketing errors instead o…\",\"oid\":\"da32e6a4326f98c6da1651ae77657347631577ec\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T17:05:58Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-29T17:05:58Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): oxfmt wrap long it.each callback signature\",\"oid\":\"3d90fbcdb515796036e5696044fdafe68860f564\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T17:10:29Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-29T17:10:29Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): regenerate OpenAPI spec for new 400 + clarified 404\",\"oid\":\"adb82e1f0fd1987f69369aeb4f67848e844fcfcc\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T17:13:50Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-29T17:13:50Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): regenerate frontend SDK for new 400 + clarified 404\",\"oid\":\"be5d9988e3a4cabbc734703c163ca9a8ef65d427\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T08:27:42Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T08:27:42Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…iene\\n\\nResilience:\\n- Promise.allSettled isolates the team-side query from the me-side: a\\n  noisy team repo no longer blanks the whole endpoint. Me-side stays\\n  load-bearing (its failure still 500s); team-side degrades to empty\\n  data with a logged span.\\n- Same isolation for the me/team mergeAnalysesInto pair.\\n- mergeAnalysesInto now wraps each per-repo getByCheckpointIds in\\n  try/catch + recordSpanError with {repoId, count} context so a single\\n  bad repo doesn't abort every subsequent lookup.\\n\\nObservability:\\n- Replace the magic \\\"unknown\\\" sentinel with the canonical\\n  LEGACY_FALLBACK_AGENT_NAME constant (\\\"Unknown\\\") so null-agent rows\\n  bucket the same way across every endpoint.\\n- Track shape-drift counters in mergeAnalysesInto (missingExtraction,\\n  missingSkillsUsed, missingMcpServersUsed, missingToolProfile) and\\n  warn-log once per request if any field is missing on most-or-all\\n  analyses — a producer schema change won't silently zero out rollups.\\n\\nType hygiene:\\n- Replace 4 hand-rolled inline Array<{...}> shapes in helpers with the\\n  canonical UserCheckpoint type. A row-shape change at the DB layer now\\n  fails at one place, not four.\\n- Derive AgentAggregate via z.infer<typeof agentAggregateSchema> so the\\n  Zod response contract and the TS type can't drift.\\n- Extract buildContributorsSection helper packaging the scoped-vs-\\n  unscoped decision in one place. The \\\"top-level summary null IFF every\\n  per-agent contributors null\\\" invariant was previously enforced inline\\n  in two places that could go out of sync. Pinned by a new test.\\n\\nTests:\\n- 4 new tests pin the new behaviors: team-side resilience (200 with\\n  empty contributors), me-side load-bearing (500), per-repo isolation\\n  in mergeAnalysesInto, contributors invariant.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"refactor(recap): address review — resilience, observability, type hyg…\",\"oid\":\"a591191f0102c92f4b0f008fe446e4d4be1bdfd6\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T09:31:15Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T09:31:15Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The drift counters in mergeAnalysesInto were over-engineering for a\\nrisk that hadn't materialized. The fields they watched (extraction,\\nskillsUsed, mcpServersUsed, toolProfile) are produced by the same\\nanalysis pipeline this codebase ships — schema drift would surface\\nin normal testing and review long before the >50%-of-analyses\\nthreshold tripped. Trading 50 lines of drift bookkeeping for a\\nnarrower function is the better deal.\\n\\nThe original silent-failure fix it was layered on top of (recordSpanError\\non malformed analysis_json) stays — that's a real anomaly worth\\nsurfacing.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"revert(recap): drop shape-drift logging on legacy aggregator\",\"oid\":\"4324d89867f35536b6b10c9e1bb1c25d730064ec\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:02:16Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:02:16Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Same audit pass that pruned PR #1737. Reverting items whose value vs\\nline-count cost didn't justify shipping on top of the partial.to-validated\\nendpoint:\\n\\nReverted:\\n- Promise.allSettled wrapping for me/team checkpoint fetches and the\\n  me/team mergeAnalysesInto pair. The team-side query has not been\\n  observed failing independently in production; the resilience layer\\n  protected against a theoretical risk and added an unwrapTeamSide /\\n  unwrapTeamSettled helper plus error-context plumbing.\\n- Per-repo try/catch in mergeAnalysesInto's getByCheckpointIds loop —\\n  same pattern: a single throw aborting the request is the\\n  partial.to-validated behavior, and an aborted analysis lookup\\n  surfaces as a 500 the outer catch handles.\\n- buildContributorsSection helper + ContribSummary / ContributorsSection\\n  interfaces. The \\\"scoped vs unscoped\\\" decision is a single inline\\n  if-else; abstracting it into a function returning both halves was\\n  weight without benefit.\\n- Four tests pinning the reverted behaviors: team-side resilience, me-\\n  side load-bearing, per-repo isolation, and contributors invariant.\\n\\nKept (real fixes from the same review pass that are cheap or correctness):\\n- LEGACY_FALLBACK_AGENT_NAME reuse — fixes a \\\"unknown\\\" vs \\\"Unknown\\\"\\n  inconsistency between this endpoint and the rest of the codebase.\\n- UserCheckpoint type replacing 4 inline shapes — DB-row type changes\\n  fail at one location now instead of four.\\n- AgentAggregate via z.infer — single source of truth between the\\n  Zod response schema and the TS type.\\n- parseRecapWindow 400 on partial / unparseable / inverted ranges —\\n  real bug (silent fallback to 6-month default).\\n- Malformed analysis_json recordSpanError — small guard against silent\\n  data corruption.\\n- buildDailyActivity UTC parsing — defensive but cheap.\\n- Integration tests for getTeamCheckpointsOnUserRepos — net-new\\n  function had zero coverage before.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"revert(recap): drop theoretical-resilience layer; keep real fixes\",\"oid\":\"281c2c1e3b3e55000facdb59dbb9cbb2268af00c\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T13:10:45Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T13:10:45Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…sers\\n\\nAddress three review comments on PR #1604.\\n\\n- Item 1: Switch the per-repo getByCheckpointIds loop in\\n  mergeAnalysesInto from a sequential `for…await` to Promise.all over\\n  byRepo. The serial loop was the dominant route latency on the\\n  no-?repo= path, where me-side can span every repo the user has\\n  activity on. Each task writes disjoint keys (rid:cp) into the shared\\n  analysesById Map, so there's no cross-task race.\\n- Item 4: distinctUsers was unconditionally `teamAuthorIds.size + 1`,\\n  over-counting when the requesting user has no checkpoints in the\\n  window for the scoped repo. Make the +1 conditional on\\n  `myCheckpoints.length > 0` and update the adjacent comment.\\n- Item 5: Hoist `import(\\\"../types\\\").StoredCheckpointAnalysis` to a\\n  normal top-of-file `import type` to match the rest of the file.\\n\\nAlso wire src/routes/recap.test.ts into vitest.unit.config.ts — it was\\nabsent from the include allowlist, so the existing 10 tests in that\\nfile were never actually running in CI.\\n\\nTests: rewrite the existing distinctUsers test as `it.each` with two\\nscenarios (user has activity, user does not) and add one new test\\nverifying the per-repo fetches are issued before either resolves\\n(deferred-promise pattern, mirroring search-index-queue.test.ts).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(recap): parallelize per-repo analyses fetch and tighten distinctU…\",\"oid\":\"b3677d21a83779f2990bbf2ea86832091bf3eb7b\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T13:15:23Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T13:15:23Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/me-recap-endpoint\",\"oid\":\"51a45963e3c97442619190dd18f49d21e285729e\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"api/docs/openapi.json\",\"additions\":460,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/activity-aggregator.test.ts\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/db/checkpoints.ts\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/db/db-types.ts\",\"additions\":9,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/planetscale/checkpoints.ts\",\"additions\":150,\"deletions\":5,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/routes/me.ts\",\"additions\":6,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.test.ts\",\"additions\":340,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"additions\":505,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"api/test/planetscale/checkpoints.test.ts\",\"additions\":96,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/vitest.unit.config.ts\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"frontend/src/gen/api-sdk/index.ts\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"frontend/src/gen/api-sdk/react-query.gen.ts\",\"additions\":22,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"frontend/src/gen/api-sdk/sdk.gen.ts\",\"additions\":8,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"frontend/src/gen/api-sdk/types.gen.ts\",\"additions\":137,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"mergedAt\":\"2026-04-30T16:22:42Z\",\"number\":1604,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"feat(api): /api/v1/me/recap endpoint for per-agent CLI aggregates\"}\n"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T13:57:55.203Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_GrhwsHDo3nFn8Cj7MJez1Tye","output":"Chunk ID: 6417d3\nWall time: 0.4651 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 7017\nOutput:\n{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFollow-up to #1604. Moves /me/recap qualitative aggregates (labels, skills, MCP servers, tool-mix, transcript tokens, files changed) out of `analysis_json` blobs and into denormalized side tables so the route can `GROUP BY` in SQL instead of fetching 1000+ rows of full JSON blobs and aggregating in JS.\\n\\n**Stacks on top of #1604** — base is `feat/me-recap-endpoint`. Once #1604 merges, GitHub auto-rebases this onto `main` and the diff shows only the perf-specific delta.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n#1604 ships /me/recap matching the /me/activity pattern (fetch checkpoints + analyses, aggregate in JS). Production-equivalent perf measurements showed `--90` recap took 60s+ on local wrangler dev — the workerd ↔ Node JSON serialization boundary doesn't scale linearly with row count, and we're shipping ~1000 analysis_json blobs per request.\\n\\nThis PR replaces that with SQL `GROUP BY` against four small denormalized facet tables. Aggregate response size drops from ~1KB-1MB of nested JSON to 5-10 rows of `(name, count)` aggregates per qualitative dimension.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\n**Schema** — four new tables, identical shape, `(repo_id, checkpoint_id, name, count)` with composite PK and a `(repo_id, name)` index for cross-checkpoint aggregation:\\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels`\\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_skills`\\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_tool_mix`\\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_mcp`\\n\\nPlus two new columns on `repo_checkpoint_analyses` for scalar aggregates: `transcript_tokens` and `files_changed`.\\n\\n**Write path** — analysis-queue worker (`generateAndStoreReview`) writes facet rows + scalar columns immediately after `markComplete` succeeds. Idempotent under retries (DELETE-then-INSERT inside a transaction for the facet tables; plain UPDATE for the scalars).\\n\\n**Read path** — `db.analyses.aggregateFacetsByAgent` does per-agent fan-out: 4 parallel facet aggregates + 1 parallel scalar SUM per agent, all via `Promise.all`. Replaces the JS-side `mergeAnalysesInto` loop in `recap.ts`.\\n\\n**Backfill** — one-off cursor-paginated script (`scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`) that reads existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json` rows, parses each blob, and upserts the derived rows. Idempotent. Supports `--dry-run` and `--limit=N`.\\n\\n**Feature flag** — `USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true` (default) routes through SQL aggregation; `=false` falls back to legacy `mergeAnalysesInto`. Kept for 24h post-deploy as a fast-rollback escape hatch (requires a redeploy to flip), removed in a follow-up.\\n\\n## Validation (on partial.to staging)\\n\\n| Range | hit1 (cold) | hit2 (warm) | hit3 (warm) |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `--day` | 2.17s | 0.91s | 0.70s |\\n| `--week` | 1.02s | 1.10s | 0.85s |\\n| `--month` | 1.40s | 1.26s | 0.92s |\\n| `--90` | 1.42s | 1.56s | 1.91s |\\n\\nAll 200s. **Backfill hasn't run on partial.to yet** — the remaining 1-2s is dominated by the upstream checkpoint queries (`getByUser`, `getTeamOnUserRepos`), unchanged from #1604. The labels/skills/tool_mix aggregation cost is already minimal.\\n\\nPre-refactor baseline: 60s+ on local wrangler. Architecture change confirmed working end-to-end on real Cloudflare Workers + real PlanetScale data.\\n\\n## Rollout sequence\\n\\n1. Merge #1604 first (slim endpoint).\\n2. Merge this PR — schema + worker writes + read path switch.\\n3. Run backfill against entire.io: `pnpm --dir api exec tsx scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`.\\n4. 24-hour soak with `USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true`. If anything's off, flip the const to `false` and redeploy.\\n5. Remove the flag + legacy `mergeAnalysesInto` in a follow-up PR.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- Mocked-route unit tests for the SQL aggregator path in `recap.test.ts`\\n- Real-MySQL integration tests for `upsertFacets`, `aggregateFacetsByCheckpointSet`, `aggregateFacetsByAgent`, and `updateScalarAggregates` in `analyses.test.ts`\\n- Worker write-path tests in `analysis-queue.test.ts` covering the `markComplete`-then-write contract and the superseded-worker no-op case\\n\\nAll passing in CI.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- migration: `api/db/migrations/20260429100000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts`\\n- types: `api/src/lib/db/db-types.ts`\\n- aggregator: `api/src/lib/planetscale/analyses.ts`\\n- worker: `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts`\\n- backfill: `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`\\n- route: `api/src/routes/recap.ts`\\n- tests across all of the above\\n\\n## Right-sizing notes\\n\\nThis PR went through an honest cost/value pass after the initial review feedback. We kept the structural wins that pay back at low line cost (`TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` shared constant, exhaustive `AnalysisFacetKind` dispatch, the small backfill bug fixes for `--limit` and narrow `catch`) and reverted the heavier review-driven additions (atomic combined-write, env-driven feature flag, parity test, full backfill test suite) because they protected against theoretical risks at meaningful line cost. The accepted tradeoffs are:\\n\\n1. **Rollback requires a redeploy, not an env flip.** The const-flag pattern is honest about this.\\n2. **Worker-side torn-write is theoretically possible** between the facet write and the scalar UPDATE. Microsecond gap, never observed in production with the existing two-write pattern.\\n3. **Backfill correctness rides on operator inspection** of resulting counts, not on automated tests of the script. It runs once.\\n\\nEach is fine for an internal analytics endpoint; would not be fine for a financial system. Documented here for the reviewer to weigh consciously.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches DB schema and the analysis write/read paths for recap; issues could cause missing/incorrect recap aggregates or added query load, though changes are largely additive and covered by tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Moves `/me/recap` qualitative aggregation from JS over `analysis_json` blobs to SQL.** This introduces four denormalized facet tables (`repo_checkpoint_analysis_{labels,skills,tool_mix,mcp}`) plus scalar columns (`transcript_tokens`, `files_changed`) on `repo_checkpoint_analyses` to enable `GROUP BY`/`SUM` queries.\\n> \\n> The analysis worker now writes facet rows and scalar aggregates after `markComplete` (idempotent delete+insert in a transaction for facets, update for scalars), and `recap.ts` switches to a new `db.analyses.aggregateFacetsByAgent` path (guarded by a temporary `USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR` constant) to populate per-agent labels/skills/tool mix/MCP + scalars without fetching full JSON.\\n> \\n> Adds a one-off backfill script to populate facets/scalars from existing `analysis_json`, expands the analyses DB namespace/types to support upsert + aggregation APIs, and updates tests to cover the new write/read paths and SQL aggregation behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 372a8ba57ffd047eeb898743eb44a7dab3ebe8c1. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-28T15:08:17Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:02:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Three tables for labels, skills, and tool-mix aggregates that today\\nlive as JSON blobs inside repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json.\\nIdentical schema across all three: (repo_id, checkpoint_id, name, count)\\nwith composite PK and a (repo_id, name) index for cross-checkpoint\\naggregation.\\n\\nEmpty until the analysis-queue worker writes to them (next chunk) and\\nthe backfill script populates historical rows.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): add denormalized analysis facet tables\",\"oid\":\"1055d937f95bbcf3c0d1ca8dac1df3df9bd8e457\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-28T15:22:03Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:02:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Wraps DELETE-then-INSERT in a transaction so consumers never see a\\ncheckpoint with partial facet rows. Idempotent — safe for the analysis\\nworker to re-call on retry, and for the backfill script to re-run.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): upsertFacets writes denormalized facet rows\",\"oid\":\"63315848e4bd39e7337e6bbeedc4e63fcfc9b010\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-28T15:27:01Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:02:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Replaces the JS-side label/skill/tool-mix counting loop. Returns\\n~5-10 rows of {name, total} regardless of how many checkpoints are\\nin the input set. Tuple-IN syntax verified to use composite PK.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): aggregateFacetsByCheckpointSet does GROUP BY in SQL\",\"oid\":\"afbc04feb1e4d863c1a3736ec48910e8a76dccae\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-28T15:52:20Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:02:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Per-agent fan-out via Promise.all over the agent set. Each agent runs\\n3 facet aggregates in parallel (one per facet kind). For typical\\n~5-agent recap responses this is 15 queries fired in 5 parallel\\nbatches of 3.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): aggregateFacetsByAgent groups facets per agent\",\"oid\":\"db2841634a104640655c7a5b351d6347ed2702ba\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-28T16:52:05Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:02:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Every completed analysis now writes denormalized rows into the three\\nfacet tables alongside the analysis_json blob. Idempotent upsertFacets\\nhandles retries cleanly.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): analysis-queue worker writes facet rows\",\"oid\":\"eb8774f7e7c41c155b7aa9dd649ee9b54aac372c\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-28T22:10:17Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:02:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Iterates repo_checkpoint_analyses where status='complete' and\\nanalysis_json is not null; parses each blob; upserts rows into the\\nthree facet tables. Cursor-paginated by (repo_id, checkpoint_id).\\nIdempotent — safe to re-run. Supports --dry-run and --limit=N.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): add backfill script for analysis facet tables\",\"oid\":\"a2fa629ac2e9edd4f15c8fd18084a164ae5b659a\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-28T22:29:23Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:44Z\",\"messageBody\":\"USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true routes through the new\\ndb.analyses.aggregateFacetsByAgent (SQL GROUP BY against the three\\nfacet tables); =false retains the legacy mergeAnalysesInto JS\\naggregator. Defaults on for the rollout; flag stays for ~24 hours\\npost-deploy as a fast-rollback escape hatch.\\n\\nReturns ~5-10 rows of pre-aggregated counts per qualitative dimension\\ninstead of 1000+ rows of analysis_json blobs. Expected ~5x prod\\nlatency improvement on /me/recap?--90; proportional improvements on\\nshorter ranges.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"perf(recap): aggregate qualitative facets in SQL (feature-flagged)\",\"oid\":\"a3d8513e31ff91babcd6e4fd63bad620b68641ce\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-28T22:41:41Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:44Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Cleanups from PR review:\\n- USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR comment now leads with REMOVE-AFTER-24h.\\n- mergeFacetsIntoAggregates clarifies that labels/skills are replaced\\n  wholesale while toolMix is overlaid for known keys only.\\n- Team-side aggregator short-circuit now has an inline comment\\n  explaining why the asymmetry with me-side is benign.\\n- Renames a recap.test.ts case to reflect what it actually tests now\\n  (the SQL aggregator pass-through rather than the original\\n  analysesById-keyed bug, which is structurally impossible under the\\n  new path).\",\"messageHeadline\":\"polish(recap): clarify feature-flag lifecycle + helper semantics\",\"oid\":\"b4ab83ccd4bf4e996979c0c039f3d9ed73a3caed\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T10:04:40Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:44Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Extends the recap perf migration to cover three fields the legacy\\nmergeAnalysesInto path filled in but the SQL aggregator silently dropped:\\nmcpServers, transcriptTokens, filesChanged. The mcp facet gets its own\\ndenormalized table (same shape as labels/skills/tool_mix); the two scalars\\nlive on repo_checkpoint_analyses directly because they're SUMs, not\\nGROUP BY name aggregates.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): add mcp facet table + scalar columns to analyses\",\"oid\":\"4a69102bd4dfa5209caac0502d1ae579faa7d1dd\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T10:04:53Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:45Z\",\"messageBody\":\"upsertFacets now writes the 4th facet kind (mcp) alongside labels/skills/\\ntool_mix in the same DELETE-then-INSERT transaction. aggregateFacetsByAgent\\nfans out 4 facet queries + 1 scalar SUM (transcript_tokens, files_changed)\\nper agent in parallel. Adds updateScalarAggregates so the worker and\\nbackfill have a single entry point for persisting the two scalars onto\\nrepo_checkpoint_analyses.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): aggregate mcp + scalar fields in SQL\",\"oid\":\"7bf52b27fff88a485732b2f47478b82a9714be79\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T10:05:04Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:45Z\",\"messageBody\":\"generateAndStoreReview now passes mcpServers (already shape-compatible from\\nextractToolMetrics) to upsertFacets and calls updateScalarAggregates with\\nthe analysis JSON's total_transcript_tokens / totalFilesChanged. Backfill\\nscript extracts the same three fields from existing analysis_json blobs so\\nalready-completed checkpoints converge.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap): worker + backfill persist mcp + scalar aggregates\",\"oid\":\"930586e00dab292c0e591d31425fcad838807580\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T10:05:12Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:45Z\",\"messageBody\":\"mergeFacetsIntoAggregates now applies all six fields the legacy path used\\nto set: labels, skills, mcpServers, toolMix, transcriptTokens, filesChanged.\\nCloses the contract regression where /me/recap was returning mcpServers=[],\\ntranscriptTokens=0, filesChanged=0 under USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(recap): surface mcpServers + scalar fields from SQL aggregator\",\"oid\":\"7331e2c2637f5186399aca10dde29ba5fb60a50e\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-29T10:09:46Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:45Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Main got a new migration (20260428152651) after we forked, so our\\nmigration's timestamp now sorts before it. CI's check-migration-order\\ncorrectly flagged this. Rename to 20260429100000 to land after main's\\nlatest. No content change.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): rename migration timestamp to sort after main\",\"oid\":\"e82f226dc2d954ca67dd714279dea88d5c077a2b\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T09:44:21Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:45Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Following a re-audit of the heavier review-feedback pass, this branch\\nretains only the items whose cost-to-value ratio justifies adding lines\\non top of partial.to-validated production code:\\n\\n- TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS shared constant (api/src/types.ts) used by both\\n  the analysis pipeline producer (extractToolMetrics) and the recap\\n  aggregator overlay consumer (mergeFacetsIntoAggregates). Replaces a\\n  hardcoded array in one site and a duplicated Set in another. Cheap\\n  guard against producer/consumer drift.\\n- Exhaustive AnalysisFacetKind dispatch in aggregateFacetsByCheckpointSet:\\n  `satisfies Record<AnalysisFacetKind, ...>` lookup map. Adding a 5th\\n  kind without extending the map is now a TS error rather than a silent\\n  fallthrough to the mcp table.\\n- Backfill script gets the two real fixes inlined: --dry-run honours\\n  --limit (advance `processed` in both branches), and the row-level\\n  catch is narrowed to SyntaxError so DB / infra errors propagate\\n  instead of being swallowed as \\\"skip and continue\\\".\\n\\nReverted (vs the previous head):\\n- Torn-write fix (persistAnalysisAggregates atomic combined method) —\\n  the gap between the two awaits is microseconds; production has\\n  shipped two-write semantics for months without incident, and the\\n  fix was theoretical hygiene, not an observed-bug fix.\\n- Env-driven ENTIRE_RECAP_LEGACY_AGGREGATOR flag — replaced an honest\\n  const kill switch with an env binding nobody is going to flip.\\n- mergeFacetsIntoAggregates warn-log — keep the shared constant guard,\\n  drop the additional log emission for a drift case that hasn't been\\n  observed.\\n- runBackfill refactor + extractFacetsFromAnalysis extraction + the\\n  227-line backfill-analysis-facets.test.ts — over-engineering for a\\n  one-shot script.\\n- Parity test in recap.test.ts — single hand-derived fixture; the\\n  equivalence claim was editorial rather than mechanical.\\n- Skip-ratio guard in backfill — narrow catch already does the work.\\n- MySQL error-code matching in migration — substring matching has been\\n  fine; migration runs once.\\n\\nNet: PR #1737 returns to the partial.to-validated worker write path\\nand const-flag pattern.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"refactor(recap-perf): keep three small review fixes; revert the rest\",\"oid\":\"3a1a4ad29aa8cf7350c8599c2be153e8c3b766be\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:31:40Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T10:31:40Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The \\\"records span error on malformed analysis_json\\\" test exercises the\\nlegacy mergeAnalysesInto path. On this branch USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true\\ngates that path off, so the test calls get(\\\"/\\\"), the SQL aggregator\\nruns, and the malformed-JSON catch never fires — the assertion that\\nrecordSpanError was called fails.\\n\\nThe fix it pins still ships on the slim PR (#1604), where the legacy\\npath IS the active path and the test runs against it. On this branch\\nthe legacy path is dead code reachable only by editing the const, so\\nthe test belongs upstream.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(recap): drop legacy-path test that's gated dead code on perf branch\",\"oid\":\"372a8ba57ffd047eeb898743eb44a7dab3ebe8c1\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T16:22:07Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T16:22:07Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Resolve conflict in api/src/routes/recap.ts: combine TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS\\nimport (head) and StoredCheckpointAnalysis import (base) into a single line.\\nBoth are still needed — TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS for the SQL-aggregator path,\\nStoredCheckpointAnalysis for the legacy mergeAnalysesInto path that the\\nUSE_FACET_AGGREGATOR flag still gates.\\n\\nUpdate \\\"issues per-repo analysis fetches in parallel\\\" test in recap.test.ts\\nto target the SQL-aggregator path. The original test (added in base) asserted\\nparallel getByCheckpointIds calls per repo, but with USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true\\ncheckpoints are bundled into a single aggregateFacetsByAgent call. The\\nparallelism contract is now between me-side and team-side aggregations,\\nwhich the rewritten test verifies.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 9b9ecb295435\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge feat/me-recap-endpoint into feat/recap-facets-sql-agg\",\"oid\":\"b909493f17132d9a1596bab0411fb39791fd51be\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T16:22:53Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T16:22:53Z\",\"messageBody\":\"aggregateFacetsByAgent in analyses.ts coalesced null agent to \\\"unknown\\\"\\n(lowercase), but aggregateCheckpointsByAgent in recap.ts coalesces null\\nagent to LEGACY_FALLBACK_AGENT_NAME (\\\"Unknown\\\", capital U). When\\nmergeFacetsIntoAggregates tried to match facet keys against the byAgent\\nmap, the lookup failed for legacy null-agent checkpoints — silently\\ndropping all facets (labels, skills, toolMix, mcpServers, transcriptTokens,\\nfilesChanged) from the response.\\n\\nSwitch aggregateFacetsByAgent to import and use LEGACY_FALLBACK_AGENT_NAME\\nso both layers agree on the same fallback string. Update the matching\\ntest to assert against the constant rather than the literal \\\"unknown\\\".\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 35ca8a17f7d2\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(recap): use LEGACY_FALLBACK_AGENT_NAME for null-agent facet grouping\",\"oid\":\"0e469964910c357b1a5fc862a3a249b86bc4cb20\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T16:31:27Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T16:31:27Z\",\"messageBody\":\"`new Map()` defaults to `Map<any, any>` and is incompatible with\\n`Map<string, never>` under tsgolint, breaking lint. The test only\\nasserts call shape and immediately resolves with empty maps, so the\\nvalue type is irrelevant — widen to `unknown` to satisfy the checker.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: cee6a1739a65\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(recap): widen deferred Map generic to unknown\",\"oid\":\"ec556e63e99de9255ac1a98c0221c993a49894a4\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-05-01T20:37:05Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-05-01T20:37:05Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…-agg\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/recap-facets-sql…\",\"oid\":\"c0bdf55458f9ff0463bcc3cf0ba21d11d25acfc1\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-05-01T20:39:19Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-05-01T20:39:19Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Main added 20260429142149 and 20260429153227 since this branch's\\n20260429100000 migration was last renamed; the migration-order CI\\ncheck requires a strictly later timestamp.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"chore(recap): bump migration timestamp past main's latest\",\"oid\":\"cb4d71102d8cf1a8481222724f8ed64f86483aed\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-05-01T20:44:51Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-05-01T20:44:51Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…-agg\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/recap-facets-sql…\",\"oid\":\"70e5a42fca057beec52d356c79cc2892054ec384\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-05-04T16:14:57Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-05-04T16:14:57Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…-agg\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/recap-facets-sql…\",\"oid\":\"c065c2a10de234f2fa1663ea89256bf100296460\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-05-04T16:58:49Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"peyton-alt\"},{\"email\":\"stefan@entire.io\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx\",\"login\":\"Soph\",\"name\":\"Stefan Haubold\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-05-04T16:58:49Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Co-authored-by: Stefan Haubold <stefan@entire.io>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Update api/src/lib/db/db-types.ts\",\"oid\":\"b3b1fcb78adb671ac5e4b1420590d848a4e2382a\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-05-04T17:05:01Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-05-04T17:05:01Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…-agg\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/recap-facets-sql…\",\"oid\":\"0dc0edcdd0416b2c2719b969de0df11d6efbd353\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-05-04T17:06:24Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-05-04T17:06:24Z\",\"messageBody\":\"GitHub web-editor commit indented at 4 spaces; oxfmt expects 2\\ninside the AnalysesNamespace interface body.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"style(recap): fix oxfmt indentation on db-types comment\",\"oid\":\"fb49089f58992924fca23a0aae75f68912f204c3\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-05-04T17:16:55Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-05-04T17:16:55Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…-agg\",\"messageHeadline\":\"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/recap-facets-sql…\",\"oid\":\"d225d899ef958b5e4d2e8f80c2d8d36c31b183ca\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"api/db/migrations/20260501120000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts\",\"additions\":72,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"api/db/schema.ts\",\"additions\":38,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts\",\"additions\":183,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/analysis-queue.test.ts\",\"additions\":338,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts\",\"additions\":58,\"deletions\":11,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/db/db-types.ts\",\"additions\":63,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/planetscale/analyses.test.ts\",\"additions\":387,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/lib/planetscale/analyses.ts\",\"additions\":200,\"deletions\":2,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.test.ts\",\"additions\":191,\"deletions\":57,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"additions\":71,\"deletions\":5,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"api/src/types.ts\",\"additions\":15,\"deletions\":8,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"mergedAt\":\"2026-05-04T17:32:50Z\",\"number\":1737,\"state\":\"MERGED\",\"title\":\"perf(recap): aggregate labels & skills in SQL\"}\n"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T13:57:55.204Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_NaO6O0CfmLWfbBsjVhdHlz6B","output":"Chunk ID: 77956b\nWall time: 0.4656 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 3553\nOutput:\n{\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire.io/trails/631\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nRecap's per-agent `toolMix`, `skills`, and `mcpServers` were Claude-shaped: the old extractor scanned raw JSONL for Claude-specific assistant/tool conventions. Codex and Gemini transcripts use different shapes, so those agents could return zeroed or incomplete tool metrics in `/api/v1/me/recap`.\\n\\nThis PR moves tool metrics onto the existing transcript-parser layer. Parsed `TranscriptMessage.toolCalls` are classified by the parser for each session's agent, so Claude, Codex, and Gemini can contribute comparable buckets without another raw-transcript scanner.\\n\\nIt also tightens `/me/recap` aggregation now that the CLI depends on this endpoint: agent keys are normalized, labels are returned with stable ids, checkpoint queries can run uncapped when no explicit limit is supplied, and session totals prefer distinct `session_ids` instead of summing checkpoint counts.\\n\\nCursor's classifier is intentionally not included here: `cursor-parser.ts` does not currently surface `toolCalls`, so adding a classifier would be dead code. Once Cursor parsing exposes calls, adding support should be a one-method parser change.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Adds optional `TranscriptParser` hooks: `classifyTool`, `extractSkillFromTool`, and `extractMcpServerFromTool`.\\n- Implements classifier/extraction hooks for Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini.\\n- Replaces the raw JSONL `extractToolMetrics` path with `extractToolMetricsFromSessions`, which consumes parsed messages and dispatches by session agent.\\n- Fixes Codex semantics:\\n  - `update_plan` is classified as `other`, not `agent`, so planning is not mixed with delegation.\\n  - MCP server names are surfaced from Codex namespace / `mcp_tool_call_end` metadata when available.\\n- Keeps Claude tool-only assistant turns so tool calls are not re-attributed to the next text-bearing assistant message.\\n- Normalizes recap agent aggregation through stable `AgentId` keys and returns `agentId` / `agentLabel` in the response.\\n- Carries `session_ids` through checkpoint queries and uses distinct session ids for recap session totals, with `session_count` as the legacy fallback.\\n- Lets recap aggregate queries run uncapped when `limit` is omitted; explicit `limit=N` still caps the query.\\n- Updates `/me/recap` aggregation and generated SDK types for the latest analysis/facet shape.\\n- Adds `scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts` to re-extract existing transcript metrics and update both:\\n  - `repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json`\\n  - denormalized facet/scalar tables used by the SQL recap aggregator\\n\\n## Pairs with\\n\\n- #1604 (recap endpoint) - merged\\n- #1737 (SQL facet aggregation) - merged\\n\\n## Rollout / Backfill\\n\\nAfter this lands, run:\\n\\n```bash\\npnpm exec tsx scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts\\n```\\n\\nThe backfill is cursor-paginated, idempotent, supports `--dry-run` and `--limit=N`, and does not make LLM calls. It preserves existing labels/scalars, rewrites only corrected tool metric fields in `analysis_json`, and keeps the facet/scalar tables in sync for rows it updates. A separate post-run facet backfill is no longer required for the corrected tool metrics.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Per-parser unit tests for Claude / Codex / Gemini classification and extraction hooks\\n- [x] Codex coverage for `update_plan` classification and MCP server metadata extraction\\n- [x] `extractToolMetricsFromSessions` regression coverage for the Codex all-zeros bug\\n- [x] Claude parser regression coverage for tool-only assistant turns\\n- [x] Recap route tests for normalized agent keys, labels, distinct session counts, uncapped aggregate queries, SQL facet aggregation, and JSON fallback\\n- [x] Checkpoint query tests for `session_ids` parsing and optional limit behavior\\n- [x] Backfill script tests for merge semantics, facet/scalar updates, dry-run behavior, and malformed JSON handling\\n- [x] `pnpm exec oxfmt --check ...`\\n- [x] `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`\\n- [x] `pnpm exec oxlint`\\n- [x] `pnpm exec vitest run --config vitest.unit.config.ts` - 60 files / 1281 tests\\n- [x] GitHub CI green: License, Checks, API, Frontend, Website\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T14:01:01Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T14:01:01Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…ier surface\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap-tools): extend TranscriptParser with optional tool classif…\",\"oid\":\"f881ac7ca2943a494a7d35910ac46b48374a3ead\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T14:09:41Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T14:09:41Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap-tools): ClaudeCodeParser exposes tool classifier (baseline)\",\"oid\":\"0324b2dc78ac319a2781e9b2745fd9b5d57b4a06\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T14:39:43Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T14:39:43Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat(recap-tools): CodexParser exposes tool classifier\",\"oid\":\"e8b3b7a7f6d71895c9fb992ce299675d4c5236b7\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-04-30T14:49:43Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"peyton@entire.io\",\"id\":\"U_kgDODuN13Q\",\"login\":\"peyton-alt\",\"name\":\"Peyton Montei\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-04-30T14:49:43Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…uristic comment\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(recap-t