{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T14:51:54.218Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_djgVUHZfLoX2HNVUEbGT3lQ6","output":"Chunk ID: 0eb55f\nWall time: 0.9023 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 3720\nOutput:\n{\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire.io/trails/6038b77becfc\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- New `GET /api/v1/me/recap` endpoint returning per-agent rollups (checkpoints, tokens, transcript tokens, files changed, labels, skills, MCP servers, tool mix) for the authenticated user, plus an optional `contributors` counterpart aggregated across every contributor on a scoped repo.\\n- Replaces three separate CLI calls (`GET /me/checkpoints` + `POST /checkpoints/analyses/batch` + `GET /:org/:repo/overview/*`) with one aggregate.\\n- Powers the \\\"you vs. team\\\" columns in `entire recap` (CLI side: entireio/cli#1015).\\n\\n## Behavior\\n\\n- **`?repo=org/name`** — when supplied, both me-side and team-side queries scope to that repo at the SQL level. The response's `contributors` field (top-level + per-agent) carries the team aggregate.\\n- **No `?repo=`** — me-side aggregates span every repo the user has checkpoints on; team-side is **skipped** entirely (no coherent \\\"everyone else\\\" reference frame across repos), and `contributors` is `null`.\\n- **`?since=…&until=…`** — ISO-8601 explicit window, takes precedence over `timeframe`. The CLI uses this so `--day`/`--week`/`--month` line up exactly with the server aggregation window.\\n- **`?timeframe=last-month|last-3-months|last-6-months`** — fallback when explicit dates are absent.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\nThis PR matches the pattern established by /me/activity (#1590): route handler in `api/src/routes/recap.ts` fetches checkpoints + analyses and aggregates qualitative fields (labels/skills/MCP/tool-mix) in JS via `mergeAnalysesInto`. ~1,500 lines, including tests + codegen output.\\n\\n**The perf refactor — denormalizing those qualitative fields into SQL-aggregatable tables — lives in #1737, stacked on this PR.** Splitting keeps each review focused: this one is \\\"add the endpoint,\\\" #1737 is \\\"make it fast.\\\" Both should land before the rollout completes.\\n\\n## Pairs with\\n\\n- CLI side: entireio/cli#1015\\n- Perf follow-up: #1737\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Live smoke vs. local wrangler dev (pointed at staging PlanetScale): `GET /api/v1/me/recap?repo=entireio/cli&since=…&until=…` returns populated agents with labels / skills / toolMix.\\n- [x] `entire recap --view both --insecure-http-auth` (CLI #1015) renders against this endpoint end-to-end.\\n- [x] `pnpm --filter entire-api run typecheck` — clean.\\n- [x] `pnpm --filter entire-api run test:run` — all tests passing.\\n- [x] `pnpm format:check` + `pnpm -r run lint` — clean.\\n\\n## Out of scope (handled in #1737)\\n\\n- Denormalized `repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels` / `_skills` / `_tool_mix` / `_mcp` tables\\n- Worker write path that populates them\\n- Backfill script for existing analyses\\n- SQL `GROUP BY` aggregator replacing `mergeAnalysesInto`\\n- `transcript_tokens` and `files_changed` scalar columns on `repo_checkpoint_analyses`\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"headRefName\":\"feat/me-recap-endpoint\",\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"6023330a30a9a3f4e21790a4538d0cf17d060e69\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-04-30T16:22:42Z\",\"number\":1604,\"title\":\"feat(api): /api/v1/me/recap endpoint for per-agent CLI aggregates\"}\n{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\nFollow-up to #1604. Moves /me/recap qualitative aggregates (labels, skills, MCP servers, tool-mix, transcript tokens, files changed) out of `analysis_json` blobs and into denormalized side tables so the route can `GROUP BY` in SQL instead of fetching 1000+ rows of full JSON blobs and aggregating in JS.\\n\\n**Stacks on top of #1604** — base is `feat/me-recap-endpoint`. Once #1604 merges, GitHub auto-rebases this onto `main` and the diff shows only the perf-specific delta.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n#1604 ships /me/recap matching the /me/activity pattern (fetch checkpoints + analyses, aggregate in JS). Production-equivalent perf measurements showed `--90` recap took 60s+ on local wrangler dev — the workerd ↔ Node JSON serialization boundary doesn't scale linearly with row count, and we're shipping ~1000 analysis_json blobs per request.\\n\\nThis PR replaces that with SQL `GROUP BY` against four small denormalized facet tables. Aggregate response size drops from ~1KB-1MB of nested JSON to 5-10 rows of `(name, count)` aggregates per qualitative dimension.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\n**Schema** — four new tables, identical shape, `(repo_id, checkpoint_id, name, count)` with composite PK and a `(repo_id, name)` index for cross-checkpoint aggregation:\\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels`\\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_skills`\\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_tool_mix`\\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_mcp`\\n\\nPlus two new columns on `repo_checkpoint_analyses` for scalar aggregates: `transcript_tokens` and `files_changed`.\\n\\n**Write path** — analysis-queue worker (`generateAndStoreReview`) writes facet rows + scalar columns immediately after `markComplete` succeeds. Idempotent under retries (DELETE-then-INSERT inside a transaction for the facet tables; plain UPDATE for the scalars).\\n\\n**Read path** — `db.analyses.aggregateFacetsByAgent` does per-agent fan-out: 4 parallel facet aggregates + 1 parallel scalar SUM per agent, all via `Promise.all`. Replaces the JS-side `mergeAnalysesInto` loop in `recap.ts`.\\n\\n**Backfill** — one-off cursor-paginated script (`scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`) that reads existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json` rows, parses each blob, and upserts the derived rows. Idempotent. Supports `--dry-run` and `--limit=N`.\\n\\n**Feature flag** — `USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true` (default) routes through SQL aggregation; `=false` falls back to legacy `mergeAnalysesInto`. Kept for 24h post-deploy as a fast-rollback escape hatch (requires a redeploy to flip), removed in a follow-up.\\n\\n## Validation (on partial.to staging)\\n\\n| Range | hit1 (cold) | hit2 (warm) | hit3 (warm) |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `--day` | 2.17s | 0.91s | 0.70s |\\n| `--week` | 1.02s | 1.10s | 0.85s |\\n| `--month` | 1.40s | 1.26s | 0.92s |\\n| `--90` | 1.42s | 1.56s | 1.91s |\\n\\nAll 200s. **Backfill hasn't run on partial.to yet** — the remaining 1-2s is dominated by the upstream checkpoint queries (`getByUser`, `getTeamOnUserRepos`), unchanged from #1604. The labels/skills/tool_mix aggregation cost is already minimal.\\n\\nPre-refactor baseline: 60s+ on local wrangler. Architecture change confirmed working end-to-end on real Cloudflare Workers + real PlanetScale data.\\n\\n## Rollout sequence\\n\\n1. Merge #1604 first (slim endpoint).\\n2. Merge this PR — schema + worker writes + read path switch.\\n3. Run backfill against entire.io: `pnpm --dir api exec tsx scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`.\\n4. 24-hour soak with `USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true`. If anything's off, flip the const to `false` and redeploy.\\n5. Remove the flag + legacy `mergeAnalysesInto` in a follow-up PR.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- Mocked-route unit tests for the SQL aggregator path in `recap.test.ts`\\n- Real-MySQL integration tests for `upsertFacets`, `aggregateFacetsByCheckpointSet`, `aggregateFacetsByAgent`, and `updateScalarAggregates` in `analyses.test.ts`\\n- Worker write-path tests in `analysis-queue.test.ts` covering the `markComplete`-then-write contract and the superseded-worker no-op case\\n\\nAll passing in CI.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- migration: `api/db/migrations/20260429100000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts`\\n- types: `api/src/lib/db/db-types.ts`\\n- aggregator: `api/src/lib/planetscale/analyses.ts`\\n- worker: `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts`\\n- backfill: `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`\\n- route: `api/src/routes/recap.ts`\\n- tests across all of the above\\n\\n## Right-sizing notes\\n\\nThis PR went through an honest cost/value pass after the initial review feedback. We kept the structural wins that pay back at low line cost (`TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` shared constant, exhaustive `AnalysisFacetKind` dispatch, the small backfill bug fixes for `--limit` and narrow `catch`) and reverted the heavier review-driven additions (atomic combined-write, env-driven feature flag, parity test, full backfill test suite) because they protected against theoretical risks at meaningful line cost. The accepted tradeoffs are:\\n\\n1. **Rollback requires a redeploy, not an env flip.** The const-flag pattern is honest about this.\\n2. **Worker-side torn-write is theoretically possible** between the facet write and the scalar UPDATE. Microsecond gap, never observed in production with the existing two-write pattern.\\n3. **Backfill correctness rides on operator inspection** of resulting counts, not on automated tests of the script. It runs once.\\n\\nEach is fine for an internal analytics endpoint; would not be fine for a financial system. Documented here for the reviewer to weigh consciously.\\n\\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\\n---\\n\\n> [!NOTE]\\n> **Medium Risk**\\n> Touches DB schema and the analysis write/read paths for recap; issues could cause missing/incorrect recap aggregates or added query load, though changes are largely additive and covered by tests.\\n> \\n> **Overview**\\n> **Moves `/me/recap` qualitative aggregation from JS over `analysis_json` blobs to SQL.** This introduces four denormalized facet tables (`repo_checkpoint_analysis_{labels,skills,tool_mix,mcp}`) plus scalar columns (`transcript_tokens`, `files_changed`) on `repo_checkpoint_analyses` to enable `GROUP BY`/`SUM` queries.\\n> \\n> The analysis worker now writes facet rows and scalar aggregates after `markComplete` (idempotent delete+insert in a transaction for facets, update for scalars), and `recap.ts` switches to a new `db.analyses.aggregateFacetsByAgent` path (guarded by a temporary `USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR` constant) to populate per-agent labels/skills/tool mix/MCP + scalars without fetching full JSON.\\n> \\n> Adds a one-off backfill script to populate facets/scalars from existing `analysis_json`, expands the analyses DB namespace/types to support upsert + aggregation APIs, and updates tests to cover the new write/read paths and SQL aggregation behavior.\\n> \\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 372a8ba57ffd047eeb898743eb44a7dab3ebe8c1. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\",\"headRefName\":\"feat/recap-facets-sql-agg\",\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"35243725c9ac52f3d662ea8f61ec8b10216a42e5\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-05-04T17:32:50Z\",\"number\":1737,\"title\":\"perf(recap): aggregate labels & skills in SQL\"}\n{\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire.io/trails/631\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nRecap's per-agent `toolMix`, `skills`, and `mcpServers` were Claude-shaped: the old extractor scanned raw JSONL for Claude-specific assistant/tool conventions. Codex and Gemini transcripts use different shapes, so those agents could return zeroed or incomplete tool metrics in `/api/v1/me/recap`.\\n\\nThis PR moves tool metrics onto the existing transcript-parser layer. Parsed `TranscriptMessage.toolCalls` are classified by the parser for each session's agent, so Claude, Codex, and Gemini can contribute comparable buckets without another raw-transcript scanner.\\n\\nIt also tightens `/me/recap` aggregation now that the CLI depends on this endpoint: agent keys are normalized, labels are returned with stable ids, checkpoint queries can run uncapped when no explicit limit is supplied, and session totals prefer distinct `session_ids` instead of summing checkpoint counts.\\n\\nCursor's classifier is intentionally not included here: `cursor-parser.ts` does not currently surface `toolCalls`, so adding a classifier would be dead code. Once Cursor parsing exposes calls, adding support should be a one-method parser change.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Adds optional `TranscriptParser` hooks: `classifyTool`, `extractSkillFromTool`, and `extractMcpServerFromTool`.\\n- Implements classifier/extraction hooks for Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini.\\n- Replaces the raw JSONL `extractToolMetrics` path with `extractToolMetricsFromSessions`, which consumes parsed messages and dispatches by session agent.\\n- Fixes Codex semantics:\\n  - `update_plan` is classified as `other`, not `agent`, so planning is not mixed with delegation.\\n  - MCP server names are surfaced from Codex namespace / `mcp_tool_call_end` metadata when available.\\n- Keeps Claude tool-only assistant turns so tool calls are not re-attributed to the next text-bearing assistant message.\\n- Normalizes recap agent aggregation through stable `AgentId` keys and returns `agentId` / `agentLabel` in the response.\\n- Carries `session_ids` through checkpoint queries and uses distinct session ids for recap session totals, with `session_count` as the legacy fallback.\\n- Lets recap aggregate queries run uncapped when `limit` is omitted; explicit `limit=N` still caps the query.\\n- Updates `/me/recap` aggregation and generated SDK types for the latest analysis/facet shape.\\n- Adds `scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts` to re-extract existing transcript metrics and update both:\\n  - `repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json`\\n  - denormalized facet/scalar tables used by the SQL recap aggregator\\n\\n## Pairs with\\n\\n- #1604 (recap endpoint) - merged\\n- #1737 (SQL facet aggregation) - merged\\n\\n## Rollout / Backfill\\n\\nAfter this lands, run:\\n\\n```bash\\npnpm exec tsx scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts\\n```\\n\\nThe backfill is cursor-paginated, idempotent, supports `--dry-run` and `--limit=N`, and does not make LLM calls. It preserves existing labels/scalars, rewrites only corrected tool metric fields in `analysis_json`, and keeps the facet/scalar tables in sync for rows it updates. A separate post-run facet backfill is no longer required for the corrected tool metrics.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n- [x] Per-parser unit tests for Claude / Codex / Gemini classification and extraction hooks\\n- [x] Codex coverage for `update_plan` classification and MCP server metadata extraction\\n- [x] `extractToolMetricsFromSessions` regression coverage for the Codex all-zeros bug\\n- [x] Claude parser regression coverage for tool-only assistant turns\\n- [x] Recap route tests for normalized agent keys, labels, distinct session counts, uncapped aggregate queries, SQL facet aggregation, and JSON fallback\\n- [x] Checkpoint query tests for `session_ids` parsing and optional limit behavior\\n- [x] Backfill script tests for merge semantics, facet/scalar updates, dry-run behavior, and malformed JSON handling\\n- [x] `pnpm exec oxfmt --check ...`\\n- [x] `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`\\n- [x] `pnpm exec oxlint`\\n- [x] `pnpm exec vitest run --config vitest.unit.config.ts` - 60 files / 1281 tests\\n- [x] GitHub CI green: License, Checks, API, Frontend, Website\\n\",\"headRefName\":\"fix/agent-aware-tool-metrics\",\"mergeCommit\":{\"oid\":\"28701d408df78877ac94aa591c4101539026326a\"},\"mergedAt\":\"2026-05-05T16:14:00Z\",\"number\":1767,\"title\":\"fix(recap): agent-aware tool metrics extraction\"}\n"}}
