{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T15:30:32.522Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_N3UzaHqKBWXPPPJ60NnHgLoE","output":"Chunk ID: 22ea09\nWall time: 1.2117 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 1373\nOutput:\n{\n  \"pull_request\": {\n    \"number\": 1157,\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1157\",\n    \"title\": \"Improve recap API error messages\",\n    \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n    \"owner\": \"entireio\",\n    \"repo\": \"cli\"\n  },\n  \"conversation_comments\": [],\n  \"reviews\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRR_kwDOQyo98M79gLaz\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"body\": \"## Pull request overview\\n\\nThis PR improves the user-facing error handling for the `entire recap` feature by switching the recap API call to the shared `api.CheckResponse` typed error path and by mapping certain API/network failures into clearer, action-oriented messages for both the static and TUI recap views.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- Replace ad-hoc HTTP error parsing in `FetchMeRecap` with `api.CheckResponse` (typed `*api.HTTPError`).\\n- Add centralized recap error-to-message mapping and use it in both the TUI error view and the static recap command path.\\n- Add unit tests covering typed unauthorized errors and the new error-message mapping behavior.\\n\\n### Reviewed changes\\n\\nCopilot reviewed 6 out of 6 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\\n\\n| File | Description |\\r\\n| ---- | ----------- |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/recap/me_recap.go | Uses `api.CheckResponse` to surface typed HTTP errors for `/me/recap`. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/recap/me_recap_test.go | New test verifying `FetchMeRecap` returns a typed 401 error with message detail. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/recap.go | Routes recap fetch failures through a new handler that can print mapped messages + return `SilentError`. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/recap_tui.go | Displays mapped recap load errors in the TUI and adds shared error mapping helpers. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/recap_tui_test.go | Adds a TUI view test ensuring 401 shows a login prompt and doesn\\u2019t render raw JSON. |\\r\\n| cmd/entire/cli/recap_test.go | Adds tests for `handleRecapFetchError` and `recapLoadErrorMessage` mappings. |\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-05-08T14:44:03Z\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"review_threads\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6Ap4P6\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/recap_tui.go\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"diffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"startLine\": null,\n      \"startDiffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"originalLine\": 241,\n      \"originalStartLine\": 237,\n      \"resolvedBy\": null,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M6_S9Oh\",\n            \"body\": \"`isRecapNetworkError` treats any `*url.Error` as a network failure, but `net/http` wraps `context.Canceled` / `context.DeadlineExceeded` in `*url.Error` as well. That can produce misleading \\u201cCould not reach entire.io\\u201d messages and trigger `SilentError` handling on cancellations/timeouts. Consider explicitly excluding context cancellation/deadlines (e.g., `errors.Is(err, context.Canceled)` / `context.DeadlineExceeded`) or checking `urlErr.Err` before classifying it as a network error.\\n\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-05-08T14:44:02Z\",\n            \"updatedAt\": \"2026-05-08T14:44:03Z\",\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6Ap4Qa\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/recap.go\",\n      \"line\": 160,\n      \"diffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"startLine\": 157,\n      \"startDiffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"originalLine\": 160,\n      \"originalStartLine\": 157,\n      \"resolvedBy\": null,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M6_S9PZ\",\n            \"body\": \"`handleRecapFetchError` prints user-facing error text to `w`, which in `newRecapCmd` is `cmd.OutOrStdout()`. This means errors will go to stdout (and into pipes/redirects), which is inconsistent with other commands that separate output vs error writers (e.g., `activity_cmd.go:52-63`). Consider passing `cmd.ErrOrStderr()` through `runRecap` and printing these mapped error messages to stderr instead.\\n\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-05-08T14:44:02Z\",\n            \"updatedAt\": \"2026-05-08T14:44:03Z\",\n            \"author\": {\n              \"login\": \"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOQyo98M6Ap4Qu\",\n      \"isResolved\": false,\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"path\": \"cmd/entire/cli/recap_tui.go\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"diffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"startLine\": null,\n      \"startDiffSide\": \"RIGHT\",\n      \"originalLine\": 244,\n      \"originalStartLine\": 203,\n      \"resolvedBy\": null,\n      \"comments\": {\n        \"nodes\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOQyo98M6_S9P3\",\n            \"body\": \"`recapLoadErrorMessage` / `recapErrorDetail` / `isRecapNetworkError` are used by both the TUI and the non-TUI path (`recap.go`), but they live in `recap_tui.go`. This makes shared error-mapping logic harder to discover and risks accidental breakage if build tags or TUI-specific refactors are introduced later. Consider moving these helpers into a shared file (e.g., `recap_errors.go`) in the `cli` package.\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-05-08T14:44:03Z\",\n            \"updatedAt\": \"2026-05-08T14:44:03Z\",\n            \"author\": {\n     