{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T17:03:06.363Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"mcp_tool_call_end","call_id":"call_x2t58TW5UzOHhZOwUgwsJGWS","invocation":{"server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_get_pr_info","arguments":{"repository_full_name":"entireio/cli","pr_number":1161}},"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":946076041},"result":{"Ok":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"url\": \"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1161\", \"number\": 1161, \"state\": \"open\", \"merged\": false, \"mergeable\": true, \"draft\": true, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\n- Show the actual recap window using the response `since`/`until` timestamps rendered in the local timezone.\\n- Show repo names in the summary context instead of only a repo count, with overflow text for larger multi-repo recaps.\\n- Add direct TUI range keys: `d` day, `w` week, `m` month, `r` 90d; keep `t` as a backward-compatible range cycle and move manual reload to `R`.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nUsers could see different recap numbers in different terminal windows because the CLI silently scoped to the current repo. The summary only said `1 repo`, which made the scoped repo invisible. The range labels also did not explain the exact local-time boundaries behind day/week/month/90d.\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n- `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache go test -count=1 ./cmd/entire/cli/recap ./cmd/entire/cli`\\n- `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-build-cache mise run lint`\\n\", \"title\": \"Clarify recap scope and range controls\", \"base\": \"main\", \"base_sha\": \"65610aff380ecaac55ee36208138fb49a540aeb3\", \"head\": \"fix-recap-context\", \"head_sha\": \"0b4335f058184f8753cebb2ddced990e58f0b831\", \"merge_commit_sha\": \"d371150b92dded90ecf77a427b7d7697decd589f\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"peyton-alt\", \"name\": \"peyton-alt\", \"email\": null, \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249787869?v=4\", \"id\": 249787869}, \"requested_reviewers\": null, \"requested_team_reviewers\": null, \"diff\": null, \"comments\": null, \"