{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T17:39:43.786Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Yes, your read is right: this is muddy.\n\nThe recap count is **not raw checkpoints** and it is **not raw commits**. It counts checkpoint rows only after they join through commit linkage:\n\n`repo_checkpoints` + `repo_checkpoint_commits` + `repo_commits`\n\nSo a checkpoint can exist in checkpoint storage but not show in recap/frontend if it never got linked to a user commit, the trailer was missing, branch sync missed it, or the `repo_commits` row is missing. The query also dedupes the same checkpoint across branches, so one checkpoint linked from multiple branches should count once.\n\nThe `Unknown` bucket is a different issue. If it shows in recap, those checkpoints are linked and counted. `Unknown` means the checkpoint row’s top-level `agent` is missing/stale/unrecognized. Labels are separate: they come from `repo_checkpoint_analyses` keyed by `(repo_id, checkpoint_id)`, so a checkpoint can have parsed analysis labels while its top-level agent is still `Unknown`.\n\nWhy “you” has Unknown labels but “team” doesn’t: counts/tokens come from checkpoint rows, but labels only appear when analysis exists and has labels. So your Unknown bucket likely has at least some complete analysis rows; the team Unknown bucket has countable checkpoint rows but no complete/label-bearing analysis rows. That’s technically explainable, but it’s a bad user-facing model.\n\nSo I think we need to test/fix three things:\n\n1. **Missing/stale agent attribution:** rehydrate or recover the agent so real analyzed checkpoints stop staying `Unknown`.\n2. **Recap fallback:** if `cp.agent` is Unknown but `sessions` metadata has real agents, recap should probably use that before making an Unknown bucket.\n3. **Missing frontend checkpoints:** separately verify whether “created but not visible” means “checkpoint exists but lacks resolved commit linkage.” That is not the same as Unknown, but it may be another API/sync issue exposed by this investigation.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
