{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T17:54:31.968Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Exactly. That mismatch is the bug.\n\nThe dashboard/checkpoint views derive agent from `sessions` metadata. Recap was grouping by the older top-level `repo_checkpoints.agent`, so stale rows with `agent = Unknown` could become “top” in recap even though the dashboard can see the real agent from the session data.\n\nI changed recap to:\n- select `sessions` and `dead_session_indices` in the recap checkpoint queries\n- resolve the recap agent from live session metadata when top-level `agent` is `Unknown`\n- use that same resolved agent for counts and labels/skills facet aggregation\n\nI also checked the other suspected stale-hydration path. That one looks like a misleading variable name, not the root cause: stale checkpoint IDs already flow into `checkpointsNeedingMetadata`. I added a guard test for that.\n\nVerification passed:\n- `pnpm exec vitest run src/lib/repo-sync-service.test.ts src/lib/planetscale/checkpoints.test.ts src/routes/recap.test.ts`\n- `pnpm --filter entire-api run typecheck`\n- `pnpm --filter entire-api run lint`\n- `pnpm run format:check`\n\nCurrent production smoke will still show the old behavior until this is deployed. After deploy/preview, rerun the same real smoke against `entire recap --static --week --color never`; if `Unknown` remains, that means those rows also lack usable `sessions` metadata and need rehydration/backfill.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
